The Funding Board consists of the four Class Representatives and is chaired by the Chair of Budgets and SIGs. The board receives and reviews all requests for funding submitted by members of the student body, both by Student Interest Groups and independent students or groups.

]The funding board requires a majority of three (3) votes in favor for a funding request or budget request to be accepted. Decisions made by the student funding board can be appealed to the Student Government Chair of Budgets and SIGs or the General Assembly.

Budget requests from SIGs should be submitted through Engage , while students or groups seeking funding can email their requests directly to the Chair of Budgets and SIGs.
